15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Composite !gure with eight panels summarizing HPV epitope\nanalyses. Panel a shows a genomic map of eight major HPV proteins indicating reading frames,\nlength, and function by color. Panel b is a bar graph of studies per HPV protein, with E6\nand E7 most referenced. Panel c is a bar graph of unique CD8+ and CD4+ epitopes per\nprotein, showing higher numbers for E6, E7, and L1. Panel d depicts epitope density by\nprotein, highlighting E6 and E7 with the highest values. Panel e displays a bar graph of\nunique epitopes per HPV genotype, with HPV16 having the most, further separated by\nepitope type and high-risk status. Panel f is a stacked bar graph of epitope distribution by\nrisk group, showing CD4+ epitopes predominate in high-risk HPV with statistical\nsigni!cance noted. Panel g is a stacked bar plot of epitope distribution by protein and risk\nstatus, illustrating high-risk dominance except in L1. Panel h is a donut chart indicating 83\npercent of epitopes are single-type and 17 percent are cross-type.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Composite figure with eight panels summarizing HPV epitope analyses. Panel a shows a genomic map of seven HPV proteins indicating reading frames, length, and function by color. Panel b is a bar graph of studies per HPV protein, with E6 and E7 most referenced. Panel c is a bar graph of unique CD8+ and CD4+ epitopes per protein, showing higher numbers for E6, E7, and L1. Panel d depicts epitope density by protein, highlighting E6 and E7 with the highest values. Panel e displays a bar graph of unique epitopes per HPV genotype, with HPV16 having the most, further separated by epitope type and high-risk status. Panel f is a stacked bar graph of epitope distribution by risk group, showing CD4+ epitopes predominate in high-risk HPV with statistical significance noted. Panel g is a stacked bar plot of epitope distribution by protein and risk status, illustrating high-risk dominance except in L1. Panel h is a donut chart indicating 83 percent of epitopes are single-type and 17 percent are cross-type.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Scientific figure with six panels summarizing response rate and HLA analysis of viral epitopes. Panel a shows a bar chart comparing positive-response rates for CD4+ and CD8+ T-cell epitopes. Panel b presents positive-response rates by HPV protein type \(oncoprotein, replication, structural\) across multiple proteins. Panel c displays numbers of unique CD4+ and CD8+ epitopes at total and restricted HLA annotation levels. Panel d bar chart shows distribution of epitopes across mono-allelic and multi-allelic HLA restriction, stratified by class. Panel e contains horizontal bar charts for unique epitope counts per HLA class I and II restricted alleles. Panel f shows scatter plots of response rate versus unique HLA allele count for CD8+ and CD4+ epitopes, colored by protein and sized by subject count.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Figure consists of five panels analyzing conservation among 485 HPV epitopes. Panel a is a scatter plot showing total HPV types covered by peptide length for CD8+ and CD4+ T cell epitopes. Panel b is a scatter plot showing HPV types covered per HPV protein with significant difference, also displaying total HPV coverage as percentages. Panel c is a bar graph of the number of epitopes for the top 40 HPV genotypes, distinguishing high-risk and low-risk groups. Panel d is a scatter plot comparing number of HPV types covered by CD4 and CD8 T cell epitopes, with a significant p value. Panel e is a set of horizontal bar charts representing predicted CD8+ and CD4+ epitopes mapped across HPV proteins and genotypes, with gray for empty multiple sequence alignment regions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Multi-panel scientific figure presents HLA prediction analysis of 485 epitopes. Panel a shows bar graphs comparing percentages of validated CD8 and CD4 epitopes with or without reported HLA restriction. Panel b displays bar charts of epitopes with exact, set, or no allele match for CD8 and CD4, highlighting statistical significance. Panel c presents the number of validated epitopes by match type for CD8 and CD4. Panel d presents bar graphs indicating the number of validated epitopes by predicted HLA binders per epitope, split by reported or unreported HLA restriction. Panel e shows the distribution of validated epitopes by HPV protein and binding predictions. Panel f contains two heatmaps displaying the top 20 CD8 and CD4 peptides and their binding strengths to various HLA alleles, color-coded by peptide function.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
